[{:db/id "q-274508/field-1/a4c8bdda186d0d425e9963bf17967cd5e356d934f319fa58135b8f8cf8a589f8" :answer/id #uuid "794bfa79-e9e8-5f66-9d8e-11d8fc80c855" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "30" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-274508/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "76891085-9a1e-5780-b53b-3bf9e217dc83" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-274508/field-1/a4c8bdda186d0d425e9963bf17967cd5e356d934f319fa58135b8f8cf8a589f8" :answer-field/choices ["q-274508/field-1/a4c8bdda186d0d425e9963bf17967cd5e356d934f319fa58135b8f8cf8a589f8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-274508/field-2/407a8c9dd7706a5c0017938bdc16d552cb404ed5280e2197eaee2471cbb5128e" :answer/id #uuid "ade23cd1-e194-580f-85b9-ec3705132ad8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "210" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-274508/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "9575f516-0acc-5c18-9b79-a4f955c7a0c5" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-274508/field-2/407a8c9dd7706a5c0017938bdc16d552cb404ed5280e2197eaee2471cbb5128e" :answer-field/choices ["q-274508/field-2/407a8c9dd7706a5c0017938bdc16d552cb404ed5280e2197eaee2471cbb5128e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-274508" :question/id #uuid "0e4a363d-d38a-53ed-83e1-c9aea0002379" :question/math-academy-id "q-274508" :question/problem "Find the solutions **in degrees** to the equation $\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-1=0$ for ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘}.$\n\n**In ascending order,** the solutions are $x=$\n{{field-1}}${}^{∘}$ and $x=$\n{{field-2}}${}^{∘}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation and isolate $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-1 & =0 \\\\ \\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =1 \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}})={30}^{∘}\n$$\n\nSince ${30}^{∘}$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}={30}^{∘}.$\n\nTo generate more solutions, we add integer multiples of ${180}^{∘}.$ Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & ={180}^{∘}+{x}_{1} \\\\  & ={180}^{∘}+{30}^{∘} \\\\  & ={210}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, in ascending order, the solutions are $x=30\\,{\\,}^{∘}$ and $x=210\\,{\\,}^{∘}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-274508/field-1" "q-274508/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0f388646-b956-518f-83df-6a49a642bd64"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-274508"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-121119/selection/622af0e9e349d6f1a4e602b749a29d77f55ffe46972d4f92917d475382528a3d" :answer/id #uuid "ce09e2d0-9123-5abb-85b7-c28d592a180d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\frac{5\\pi }{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121119/selection/55101f0b4888077918226a8b3669d10043f6ee9773318bcd5c63a35ef36100fd" :answer/id #uuid "c9a1e997-df29-5cf1-951f-f9868235631f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\frac{2\\pi }{3},\\frac{5\\pi }{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121119/selection/c57c39367a85845de5cbee30b2f9ea57dcdbf816ab179fdcdd61a27f24c26ff4" :answer/id #uuid "f849dc82-cff0-5379-98d0-5d57e99be843" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\frac{3\\pi }{4},\\frac{5\\pi }{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121119/selection/cfef9acaa50d52a14758d2e4ae5334697ec046bff180207fd7a693101464c15f" :answer/id #uuid "94b3a771-ad77-555f-8969-4c9ee99117c0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\frac{2\\pi }{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121119/selection/614ed68495b64af8ec0e7df520ef4d752647d6d96b370efa311048a55189b704" :answer/id #uuid "0e7952ae-af35-5750-a059-6b2e161687a1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{3\\pi }{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121119/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ecb8e0f4-e168-500b-bf2b-e5e2dcb5f9aa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-121119/selection/55101f0b4888077918226a8b3669d10043f6ee9773318bcd5c63a35ef36100fd" :answer-field/choices ["q-121119/selection/622af0e9e349d6f1a4e602b749a29d77f55ffe46972d4f92917d475382528a3d" "q-121119/selection/55101f0b4888077918226a8b3669d10043f6ee9773318bcd5c63a35ef36100fd" "q-121119/selection/c57c39367a85845de5cbee30b2f9ea57dcdbf816ab179fdcdd61a27f24c26ff4" "q-121119/selection/cfef9acaa50d52a14758d2e4ae5334697ec046bff180207fd7a693101464c15f" "q-121119/selection/614ed68495b64af8ec0e7df520ef4d752647d6d96b370efa311048a55189b704"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-121119" :question/id #uuid "b26e4756-90f6-541a-8bf3-78caf4240c2f" :question/math-academy-id "q-121119" :question/problem "Solve the equation $7\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+2\\sqrt{3}=-5\\sqrt{3}$ for $0\\le x<2\\pi .$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation and isolate $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+2\\sqrt{3} & =-5\\sqrt{3} \\\\ 7\\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =-7\\sqrt{3} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =-\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-\\sqrt{3})=-\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $-\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ lies outside the given domain, it is not a solution.\n\nTo generate more solutions, we add integer multiples of $\\pi .$ Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =\\pi +x=\\pi +(-\\frac{\\pi }{3})=\\frac{2\\pi }{3}, \\\\ {x}_{2} & =2\\pi +x=2\\pi +(-\\frac{\\pi }{3})=\\frac{5\\pi }{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solutions are $x=\\frac{2\\pi }{3},\\frac{5\\pi }{3}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-121119/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0f388646-b956-518f-83df-6a49a642bd64"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-121119"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-321345/field-1/23a7b929cccc5bdeb88db3bdc770afbaf59570d63e930fc5c94f26cb6f5091dc" :answer/id #uuid "988e2290-bcd6-52be-b3a6-9e2ba1dcf375" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "60" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-321345/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "a148d82a-6f80-5c65-a38c-751445abda9b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-321345/field-1/23a7b929cccc5bdeb88db3bdc770afbaf59570d63e930fc5c94f26cb6f5091dc" :answer-field/choices ["q-321345/field-1/23a7b929cccc5bdeb88db3bdc770afbaf59570d63e930fc5c94f26cb6f5091dc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-321345/field-2/557015e94af5fa4bd02ae0ff131d8572cb165f5648829317508c9b9e01215bfe" :answer/id #uuid "b6017ea7-438d-5b90-b1bd-4b0fe2f4f049" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "240" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-321345/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "748ffd06-1180-5721-8833-6dad91ea3e3c" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-321345/field-2/557015e94af5fa4bd02ae0ff131d8572cb165f5648829317508c9b9e01215bfe" :answer-field/choices ["q-321345/field-2/557015e94af5fa4bd02ae0ff131d8572cb165f5648829317508c9b9e01215bfe"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-321345" :question/id #uuid "4e6bb08d-3b84-539c-a7fd-00e965243df2" :question/math-academy-id "q-321345" :question/problem "Find the solutions **in degrees** to the equation $2\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-2\\sqrt{3}=0$ for ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘}.$\n\n**In ascending order,** the solutions are $x=$\n{{field-1}}${}^{∘}$ and $x=$\n{{field-2}}${}^{∘}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation and isolate $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-2\\sqrt{3} & =0 \\\\ 2\\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =2\\sqrt{3} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=arctan\\,(\\sqrt{3})={60}^{∘}\n$$\n\nSince ${60}^{∘}$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}={60}^{∘}.$\n\nTo generate more solutions, we add integer multiples of ${180}^{∘}.$ Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & ={180}^{∘}+{x}_{1} \\\\  & ={180}^{∘}+{60}^{∘} \\\\  & ={240}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, in ascending order, the solutions are $x=60\\,{\\,}^{∘}$ and $x=240\\,{\\,}^{∘}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-321345/field-1" "q-321345/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0f388646-b956-518f-83df-6a49a642bd64"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-321345"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-321292/field-1/d569d64e1b94dabdc9f89c1070c848c6c96526a20f320d6b4971ae3a32604bcf" :answer/id #uuid "eed7bdd9-bb61-57fd-b6de-f955cfa8bc05" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2\\pi}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-321292/field-1/ccc5b7f3cfdb4c2dfc0e1f31be54559a1ab3adaf142e500fc1f1b7bc87e93b08" :answer/id #uuid "b915c3fc-977c-5d0b-a46d-bc5462d4b2a9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-321292/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "235d7247-3fae-5bee-9fb4-fa464187a226" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-321292/field-1/d569d64e1b94dabdc9f89c1070c848c6c96526a20f320d6b4971ae3a32604bcf" :answer-field/choices ["q-321292/field-1/d569d64e1b94dabdc9f89c1070c848c6c96526a20f320d6b4971ae3a32604bcf" "q-321292/field-1/ccc5b7f3cfdb4c2dfc0e1f31be54559a1ab3adaf142e500fc1f1b7bc87e93b08"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-321292/field-2/30c65f95461d7cf832bda679931de2b4099e743d19de1b695cb0707c6a50ede3" :answer/id #uuid "2530d4ff-120d-58d4-a9d2-8b1ebfb2d585" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5\\pi}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-321292/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "91136653-2103-5f86-afeb-9e183499d2f2" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-321292/field-2/30c65f95461d7cf832bda679931de2b4099e743d19de1b695cb0707c6a50ede3" :answer-field/choices ["q-321292/field-2/30c65f95461d7cf832bda679931de2b4099e743d19de1b695cb0707c6a50ede3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-321292" :question/id #uuid "57779c0f-dbe5-516f-bc87-10d3b3bb9965" :question/math-academy-id "q-321292" :question/problem "Find the **exact solutions in radians** to the equation $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=-\\sqrt{3}$ for $0\\le x<2\\pi .$\n\n**In ascending order,** the solutions are $x=$ \n{{field-1}}\nand $x=$ \n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-\\sqrt{3})=-\\frac{\\pi }{3}\n$$\n\nSince $-\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ lies outside the given domain its not a solution.\n\nTo generate the solutions, we add integer multiples of $\\pi .$ Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =\\pi +x=\\pi -\\frac{\\pi }{3}=\\frac{2\\pi }{3}, \\\\ {x}_{2} & =2\\pi +x=2\\pi +\\frac{\\pi }{3}=\\frac{5\\pi }{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, in ascending order, the solutions are $x=\\frac{2\\pi }{3}$ and $x=\\frac{5\\pi }{3}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-321292/field-1" "q-321292/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0f388646-b956-518f-83df-6a49a642bd64"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-321292"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-321347/field-1/42aff35720b567089407a2a0cf7c70ff6334c9493e4d877ecdcdfa86adae004c" :answer/id #uuid "a36dcdf3-791d-57f1-a976-493e0f834822" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "150" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-321347/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "da7ba1a8-3e0f-54b6-bc49-d0ca7d4edcc9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-321347/field-1/42aff35720b567089407a2a0cf7c70ff6334c9493e4d877ecdcdfa86adae004c" :answer-field/choices ["q-321347/field-1/42aff35720b567089407a2a0cf7c70ff6334c9493e4d877ecdcdfa86adae004c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-321347/field-2/6d5e653a0cc5c6e6fc44c5c3386727c89009586dc5171332dccb4c794ca30987" :answer/id #uuid "011b1516-acab-5c2c-9060-faec17381111" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "330" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-321347/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "86485b49-6eed-5a6e-a6c3-8a4ece4b51d1" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-321347/field-2/6d5e653a0cc5c6e6fc44c5c3386727c89009586dc5171332dccb4c794ca30987" :answer-field/choices ["q-321347/field-2/6d5e653a0cc5c6e6fc44c5c3386727c89009586dc5171332dccb4c794ca30987"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-321347" :question/id #uuid "b702e76f-8945-5678-825a-81c99d35b854" :question/math-academy-id "q-321347" :question/problem "Find the solutions **in degrees** to the equation $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}=0$ for ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘}.$\n\n**In ascending order,** the solutions are $x=$\n{{field-1}}${}^{∘}$ and $x=$\n{{field-2}}${}^{∘}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation and isolate $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} & =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=arctan\\,(-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}})=-{30}^{∘}\n$$\n\nSince $-{30}^{∘}$ is outside the given domain, it is not a solution.\n\nTo generate the solutions, we add integer multiples of ${180}^{∘}.$ Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & ={180}^{∘}+(-{30}^{∘})={150}^{∘}, \\\\ {x}_{2} & ={360}^{∘}+(-{30}^{∘})={330}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, in ascending order, the solutions are $x=150\\,{\\,}^{∘}$ and $x=330\\,{\\,}^{∘}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-321347/field-1" "q-321347/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0f388646-b956-518f-83df-6a49a642bd64"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-321347"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-321831/field-1/59afba529b533d43da0939a1f2e3244430951f512675b31bbaaa22a58d5faf55" :answer/id #uuid "110fc367-7dda-5b28-ab9b-352ae0a2466f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-321831/field-1/2ab4d887bd03c06472fa528766bb206551766ecc540c0548c4b29ee1879c735d" :answer/id #uuid "ca3ed868-ac15-5829-9f62-445e5fab8750" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-321831/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "cd7d8fc6-7441-50c9-aeb2-5523e2310f8e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-321831/field-1/59afba529b533d43da0939a1f2e3244430951f512675b31bbaaa22a58d5faf55" :answer-field/choices ["q-321831/field-1/59afba529b533d43da0939a1f2e3244430951f512675b31bbaaa22a58d5faf55" "q-321831/field-1/2ab4d887bd03c06472fa528766bb206551766ecc540c0548c4b29ee1879c735d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-321831/field-2/e9620baa28e05f7c44f36afdaf8b68de179a6da79151d2968afccf22698b9338" :answer/id #uuid "022972ae-9bf9-567a-b3d4-a9ba985a7e82" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5.3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-321831/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "69a9f44f-1bfa-5831-8c74-2b3d1ecb8c07" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-321831/field-2/e9620baa28e05f7c44f36afdaf8b68de179a6da79151d2968afccf22698b9338" :answer-field/choices ["q-321831/field-2/e9620baa28e05f7c44f36afdaf8b68de179a6da79151d2968afccf22698b9338"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-321831" :question/id #uuid "4d543f07-f315-5493-a1f8-89213f5f2dee" :question/math-academy-id "q-321831" :question/problem "Find the solutions **in radians** to the equation $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+2=0.5$ for $0\\le x<2\\pi .$ Round your answers to **one decimal place**.\n\n**In ascending order,** the solutions are $x=$\n{{field-1}}\nand $x=$ \n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation and isolate $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+2 & =0.5 \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =-1.5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-1.5)=-0.982\\,794…≈-1.0\n$$\n\nSince $-1.0$ lies outside the given domain, it is not a solution.\n\nTo generate solutions in the domain, we add integer multiples of $\\pi .$ Hence,\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=\\pi +(-0.982\\,794…)≈2.2,\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}=2\\pi +(-0.982\\,794…)≈5.3.\n$$\n\nSo, in ascending order and rounded to one decimal place, the solutions are $x=2.2$ and $x=5.3.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-321831/field-1" "q-321831/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d8c7ab50-5a8b-5bcd-8483-cec8bf6bd3ce"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-321831"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-321725/field-1/0e8c61e1cbe5b6d4b3e52c0431e48b853c5faa01ca7ca0f5f9cf780292b06b1f" :answer/id #uuid "5a523010-30af-5dfb-866d-3823347f57c1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-321725/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "0d59f953-f214-5f32-be00-d46351abe97f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-321725/field-1/0e8c61e1cbe5b6d4b3e52c0431e48b853c5faa01ca7ca0f5f9cf780292b06b1f" :answer-field/choices ["q-321725/field-1/0e8c61e1cbe5b6d4b3e52c0431e48b853c5faa01ca7ca0f5f9cf780292b06b1f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-321725/field-2/e69e46056c61d03ac81fa66e418618e77f184bfb88b9bbf8c04a941cc85eaec1" :answer/id #uuid "3c0219bf-f213-539e-bea3-96788d5ca7fa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3.8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-321725/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "f4072c17-cf94-5797-b3ff-b701ab8e898d" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-321725/field-2/e69e46056c61d03ac81fa66e418618e77f184bfb88b9bbf8c04a941cc85eaec1" :answer-field/choices ["q-321725/field-2/e69e46056c61d03ac81fa66e418618e77f184bfb88b9bbf8c04a941cc85eaec1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-321725" :question/id #uuid "d722d701-1483-5b11-9d46-d8313fd03803" :question/math-academy-id "q-321725" :question/problem "Find the solutions **in radians** to the equation $4\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-3=0$ for $0\\le x<2\\pi .$ Round your answers to **one decimal place**.\n\n**In ascending order,** the solutions are $x=$\n{{field-1}}\nand $x=$ \n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation and isolate $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-3 & =0 \\\\ 4\\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =3 \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =\\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{3}{4})=0.643\\,501…≈0.6\n$$\n\nSince $0.6$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}=0.6.$\n\nTo generate solutions in the domain, we add integer multiples of $\\pi .$ Hence,\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}=\\pi +0.643\\,501…≈3.8.\n$$\n\nSo, in ascending order and rounded to one decimal place, the solutions are $x=0.6$ and $x=3.8.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-321725/field-1" "q-321725/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d8c7ab50-5a8b-5bcd-8483-cec8bf6bd3ce"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-321725"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-121264/selection/596d94af4f340501f3e78aef98f20843a1dca3ee2d589030cb5370af6c4c1c37" :answer/id #uuid "9144e89e-5100-5e9d-8661-2edd52be6f10" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x={71}^{∘},{251}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121264/s