wer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x={69}^{∘},{249}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121130/selection/7a7afdc893485e99a9fda56ac0c68e82af4fab655575795ca4fa9c5accb154ef" :answer/id #uuid "3e863113-e050-5e61-8a8c-85b2d57826af" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x={65}^{∘},{245}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121130/selection/05bfa08c7c4307ab4513d066f54b1b04f854b690dbd797054a25a50b84f07916" :answer/id #uuid "1e024257-6d61-51eb-b36f-10514fa1c377" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x={85}^{∘},{265}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121130/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a8bdec1e-5039-50b4-9d7c-35a12b29d275" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-121130/selection/05bfa08c7c4307ab4513d066f54b1b04f854b690dbd797054a25a50b84f07916" :answer-field/choices ["q-121130/selection/eaf167848f39c86d26f23c39f189891f37594447d441b21522a0da34086ef99c" "q-121130/selection/f9b3777a7ebd22df965f2a6418aa92034bc81148541b4a9f93ca33417df37bcb" "q-121130/selection/5cff720bc8785ce843623b6fe8241c74a674e00b5f6ee81fef9adad9cb3dd405" "q-121130/selection/7a7afdc893485e99a9fda56ac0c68e82af4fab655575795ca4fa9c5accb154ef" "q-121130/selection/05bfa08c7c4307ab4513d066f54b1b04f854b690dbd797054a25a50b84f07916"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-121130" :question/id #uuid "0e51ee52-43c9-52c5-87d3-c93144f63c70" :question/math-academy-id "q-121130" :question/problem "Solve the equation $3\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-33=0$ for ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘},$ rounded to the nearest integer." :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation and isolate $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-33=0 \\\\ 3\\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =33 \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext,  we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(11)=84.805\\,571{…}^{∘}≈{84.81}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince ${84.81}^{∘}$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}={84.81}^{∘}.$\n\nTo generate more solutions, we add integer multiples of ${180}^{∘}.$ Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2}={180}^{∘}+{84.81}^{∘}={264.81}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solutions are\n\n$$\nx={85}^{∘},{265}^{∘}\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-121130/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d8c7ab50-5a8b-5bcd-8483-cec8bf6bd3ce"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-121130"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-321879/field-1/d2e5ac5d5dcba192fcba3a9943cd198d6d54ef2b54bcd6689f92dfae1fe7cd91" :answer/id #uuid "d3754d64-d59b-5c6c-a6de-c6657aeea82d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-321879/field-1/438469ab2d71e1bb8b63f3164bacb1bbb54e29062b14dce6a666b63ac0081609" :answer/id #uuid "9bb9ad3d-2c6c-534a-bbf8-8737929fde6a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-321879/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "31b632ab-5141-545a-a657-232bbe0f540a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-321879/field-1/d2e5ac5d5dcba192fcba3a9943cd198d6d54ef2b54bcd6689f92dfae1fe7cd91" :answer-field/choices ["q-321879/field-1/d2e5ac5d5dcba192fcba3a9943cd198d6d54ef2b54bcd6689f92dfae1fe7cd91" "q-321879/field-1/438469ab2d71e1bb8b63f3164bacb1bbb54e29062b14dce6a666b63ac0081609"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-321879/field-2/09f471dae983db28c0826657524c52e39160889c30208ec0dd3cf10ef9c2407a" :answer/id #uuid "8b4ce3c5-ffed-5092-a7fa-cf751d3f4dd9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5\\pi}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-321879/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "aa1a1e47-0fad-52ec-9936-8ef201c5f389" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-321879/field-2/09f471dae983db28c0826657524c52e39160889c30208ec0dd3cf10ef9c2407a" :answer-field/choices ["q-321879/field-2/09f471dae983db28c0826657524c52e39160889c30208ec0dd3cf10ef9c2407a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-321879" :question/id #uuid "51a0110b-2df6-56e3-9d5a-094cffde5bcf" :question/math-academy-id "q-321879" :question/problem "Find the **exact solutions in radians** to the equation $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}$ for $-\\pi <x\\le \\pi .$\n\n**In ascending order,** the solutions are $x=$\n{{field-1}} and $x=$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=arctan\\,(-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}})=-\\frac{\\pi }{6}\n$$\n\nSince $-\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}=-\\frac{\\pi }{6}.$\n\nTo generate more solutions, we add integer multiples of $\\pi .$ Hence,\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}=\\pi +{x}_{1}=\\pi -\\frac{\\pi }{6}=\\frac{5\\pi }{6}.\n$$\n\nSo, in ascending order, the solutions are $x=-\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ and $x=\\frac{5\\pi }{6}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-321879/field-1" "q-321879/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ebf8592e-1a43-5d65-af3c-9becd79ae8b9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-321879"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-274523/field-1/845beb42e162b04150b7b438e2c57c85fb9c5dc5bb6c7f2891f90687bf680708" :answer/id #uuid "424803f4-87be-5f34-ab1e-acf42aecc55a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-30" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-274523/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "8590ccc9-cfcb-5318-997e-3f893c961346" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-274523/field-1/845beb42e162b04150b7b438e2c57c85fb9c5dc5bb6c7f2891f90687bf680708" :answer-field/choices ["q-274523/field-1/845beb42e162b04150b7b438e2c57c85fb9c5dc5bb6c7f2891f90687bf680708"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-274523/field-2/42aff35720b567089407a2a0cf7c70ff6334c9493e4d877ecdcdfa86adae004c" :answer/id #uuid "f62e37e4-70f2-5f79-9cd1-409293dce939" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "150" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-274523/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "16205a8b-891b-52be-88a1-9081088162f6" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-274523/field-2/42aff35720b567089407a2a0cf7c70ff6334c9493e4d877ecdcdfa86adae004c" :answer-field/choices ["q-274523/field-2/42aff35720b567089407a2a0cf7c70ff6334c9493e4d877ecdcdfa86adae004c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-274523" :question/id #uuid "6ce4a7c1-f895-54e6-aeab-6c701b4779c4" :question/math-academy-id "q-274523" :question/problem "Find the solutions **in degrees** to the equation $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}$ for $-{180}^{∘}<x\\le {180}^{∘}.$\n\n**In ascending order,** the solutions are $x=$\n{{field-1}}${}^{∘}$ and $x=$\n{{field-2}}${}^{∘}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3})=-{30}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nSince $-{30}^{∘}$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}=-{30}^{∘}.$\n\nTo generate more solutions, we add integer multiples of ${180}^{∘}.$ Hence,\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}={180}^{∘}+{x}_{1}={180}^{∘}-{30}^{∘}={150}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nSo, in ascending order, the solutions are $x=-30\\,{\\,}^{∘}$ and $x=150\\,{\\,}^{∘}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-274523/field-1" "q-274523/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ebf8592e-1a43-5d65-af3c-9becd79ae8b9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-274523"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-321896/field-1/a39e4c3855e119cc134cd501616b2d4242dd33fe6134da1d7da0776d673411f7" :answer/id #uuid "2fcc9d8a-9d25-5f0d-81c7-3b5d148bd28d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-0.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-321896/field-1/95a1d5fa369c4d08bda10228102d0fbae8f93732afc4c2ec3773c4f3d47df28c" :answer/id #uuid "90b60439-822c-58a3-bcff-35aebe0be636" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-321896/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "7625f163-4507-568d-ac7b-3f567a86f4b6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-321896/field-1/a39e4c3855e119cc134cd501616b2d4242dd33fe6134da1d7da0776d673411f7" :answer-field/choices ["q-321896/field-1/a39e4c3855e119cc134cd501616b2d4242dd33fe6134da1d7da0776d673411f7" "q-321896/field-1/95a1d5fa369c4d08bda10228102d0fbae8f93732afc4c2ec3773c4f3d47df28c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-321896/field-2/449eabead9e7713acaede5d2afc64373661ad92a6819ce95b943eb2835d0094c" :answer/id #uuid "b301e7ba-1d40-5def-8eb8-0f549dd58ec5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-321896/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "ab955803-2746-5eef-a691-38a6d6318efe" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-321896/field-2/449eabead9e7713acaede5d2afc64373661ad92a6819ce95b943eb2835d0094c" :answer-field/choices ["q-321896/field-2/449eabead9e7713acaede5d2afc64373661ad92a6819ce95b943eb2835d0094c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-321896" :question/id #uuid "d15bb307-cc1d-5861-9298-e5a7bd9d8b8f" :question/math-academy-id "q-321896" :question/problem "Find the solutions **in radians** to the equation $2\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+1=0$ for $-\\pi <x\\le \\pi .$ Round your answers to **one decimal place**.\n\n**In ascending order,** the solutions are $x=$\n{{field-1}} and $x=$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation and isolate $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+1 & =0 \\\\ 2\\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =-1 \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =-0.5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-0.5)=-0.463\\,647…≈-0.5\n$$\n\nSince $-0.5$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}=-0.5$\n\nTo generate more solutions, we add integer multiples of $\\pi .$ Hence,\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}=\\pi +(-0.463\\,647…)=2.677\\,945…≈2.7.\n$$\n\nSo, in ascending order and rounded to one decimal place, the solutions are $x=-0.5$ and $x=2.7.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-321896/field-1" "q-321896/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ebf8592e-1a43-5d65-af3c-9becd79ae8b9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-321896"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-121332/selection/2f5552f585fe52d7f6a9f24fa4665876a0fc78728d77505d0144c3a25ea6ff7a" :answer/id #uuid "c7f414ec-c23e-5c94-a1ef-cc5ac0d12b70" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5\\,300" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121332/selection/ba5e98e67e82d8297ce1200b72cc481a2cddb37806fd6551b6166f3455749b2a" :answer/id #uuid "81efa90b-43dc-5032-80c8-9e3077034f82" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3\\,600" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121332/selection/5d48d61366a04ac58d2337711d11ca387ef67d954e4fbe520f47d1d6b41aea85" :answer/id #uuid "bef1c2d1-4e66-59d1-bdaf-9f5f726d2934" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-8\\,300" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121332/selection/d38b1f098e5b80effd70b36a79cbcb66ceca282fb7be3553aabed3877daf5dec" :answer/id #uuid "994c292f-1380-58e3-bc58-04f84532ce4e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4\\,500" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121332/selection/11ac09f2c5173af1077a9aa81cf4c1d7e59a1929bbd1eb264e6eb9b6448596b3" :answer/id #uuid "a94023f5-c2de-53f3-99d1-0122ee6a1352" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1\\,600" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121332/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "39335906-7965-5b7b-b39c-0f411fbdcdcb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-121332/selection/d38b1f098e5b80effd70b36a79cbcb66ceca282fb7be3553aabed3877daf5dec" :answer-field/choices ["q-121332/selection/2f5552f585fe52d7f6a9f24fa4665876a0fc78728d77505d0144c3a25ea6ff7a" "q-121332/selection/ba5e98e67e82d8297ce1200b72cc481a2cddb37806fd6551b6166f3455749b2a" "q-121332/selection/5d48d61366a04ac58d2337711d11ca387ef67d954e4fbe520f47d1d6b41aea85" "q-121332/selection/d38b1f098e5b80effd70b36a79cbcb66ceca282fb7be3553aabed3877daf5dec" "q-121332/selection/11ac09f2c5173af1077a9aa81cf4c1d7e59a1929bbd1eb264e6eb9b6448596b3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-121332" :question/id #uuid "09744146-6a55-5a6c-9779-7507baea6402" :question/math-academy-id "q-121332" :question/problem "Given that ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the solutions of the equation $3\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+1=4$  for $-{180}^{∘}<x\\le {180}^{∘},$ what is the numerical value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation and isolate $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+1 & =4 \\\\ 3\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =3 \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3})={30}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince ${30}^{∘}$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}={30}^{∘}.$\n\nTo generate more solutions, we add integer multiples of ${180}^{∘}.$ Hence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2}=-{180}^{∘}+{x}_{1}=-{180}^{∘}+{30}^{∘}=-{150}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solutions are $x=-{150}^{∘},{30}^{∘}.$\n\nFinally, the numerical value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}$ is\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=-150\\cdot 30=-4\\,500.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-121332/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ebf8592e-1a43-5d65-af3c-9becd79ae8b9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-121332"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-321883/field-1/6ac7f16e90d3eb712680917d4ccc1d5afb8ca7b654c995be03089c8f1695244a" :answer/id #uuid "ed9c1b5b-e708-51e7-9461-fa69d1b1c641" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1.7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-321883/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "11b0d4a5-089d-5b82-92ad-fcd655cb46c6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-321883/field-1/6ac7f16e90d3eb712680917d4ccc1d5afb8ca7b654c995be03089c8f1695244a" :answer-field/choices ["q-321883/field-1/6ac7f16e90d3eb712680917d4ccc1d5afb8ca7b654c995be03089c8f1695244a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-321883/field-2/55a4398ff2bb390f50308343800529dea9dc0d15acc52b6cb929bee17c075b16" :answer/id #uuid "c16566ef-3f96-514f-a73e-4cfd21482f07" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-321883/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "a18ea6fb-8e0d-5387-8357-d92855007b54" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-321883/field-2/55a4398ff2bb390f50308343800529dea9dc0d15acc52b6cb929bee17c075b16" :answer-field/choices ["q-321883/field-2/55a4398ff2bb390f50308343800529dea9dc0d15acc52b6cb929bee17c075b16"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-321883" :question/id #uuid "d08b21d6-0805-5be8-81c9-ccbf852affe2" :question/math-academy-id "q-321883" :question/problem "Find the solutions **in radians** to the equation $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=7$ for $-\\pi <x\\le \\pi .$ Round your answers to **one decimal place**.\n\n**In ascending order,** the solutions are $x=$\n{{field-1}} and $x=$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(7)=1.428\\,899…≈1.4\n$$\n\nSince $1.4$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}=1.4.$\n\nTo generate more solutions, we add integer multiples of $\\pi .$ Hence,\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}=-\\pi +{x}_{1}=-\\pi +1.428\\,899…≈-1.7.\n$$\n\nSo, in ascending order and rounded to one decimal place, the solutions are $x=-1.7$ and $x=1.4.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-321883/field-1" "q-321883/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ebf8592e-1a43-5d65-af3c-9becd79ae8b9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-321883"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-322701/field-1/7e35823d10f65dabc95929142749aca3c62d1af7b6ab33b0ab3042beceb457c5" :answer/id #uuid "723224dc-4baa-565e-b25a-1eafdd8e5a4f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{11\\pi}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-322701/field-1/09f471dae983db28c0826657524c52e39160889c30208ec0dd3cf10ef9c2407a" :answer/id #uuid "89bfcde6-510f-520f-a35f-be09e4e13a54" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5\\pi}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-322701/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "89517520-5831-5f1e-9edb-49bc2f2a025d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-322701/field-1/7e35823d10f65dabc95929142749aca3c62d1af7b6ab33b0ab3042beceb457c5" :answer-field/choices ["q-322701/field-1/7e35823d10f65dabc95929142749aca3c62d1af7b6ab33b0ab3042beceb457c5" "q-322701/field-1/09f471dae983db28c0826657524c52e39160889c30208ec0dd3cf10ef9c2407a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-322701" :question/id #uuid "fa7635fe-efad-5976-a9f0-503e368f4d30" :question/math-academy-id "q-322701" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13952589/assets/e03611d72e1c88d1e49806ede117b6808186de27346e426104dca69391f29bbf.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the curve $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x$ and the line $y=-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}.$\n\nThe **exact** value of the $x$-coordinate of the point $A$ is \n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The $y$-values of both functions are the same at the intersection point. Equating the two equations gives:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=arctan\\,(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3})=-\\frac{\\pi }{6}\n$$\n\nThis value lies outside $\\frac{3\\pi }{2}<x<\\frac{5\\pi }{2}.$ To get a value that's inside the required domain, we add $2\\pi $ to the principal value. Thus,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & =x+2\\pi  \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\pi }{6}+2\\pi  \\\\  & =\\frac{11\\pi }{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the $x$-coordinate of $A$ is $\\frac{11\\pi }{6}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-322701/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a71da663-e7a4-5781-973c-5dc7e4deb83f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-322701"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-121545/selection/0f2229a8d284b0e3be30b8a234f6bf87fcbd918a8d02f5bb5f6312388d0ca00a" :answer/id #uuid "ce68ef0f-3cb2-5124-85b3-d207736d1ca3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{5\\pi }{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121545/selection/8642f29c07ed588847b818ca52d7d9b13f60105c8ca35b3f5cb1a649a54ead1c" :answer/id #uuid "ae4b1db6-69f0-5280-b7f3-38aa8d055c17" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121545/selection/2bc5d83371a24844476947c013c304745bdc01e4bc7ab45335b74b409478e254" :answer/id #uuid "f5fa732c-faac-5309-917d-db998fef904d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{4\\pi }{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121545/selection/f877c20246cdffb02c0bf1049751cbded026a1167735517391df4b4eb845057e" :answer/id #uuid "d369c9f5-9662-5cd1-868d-408562a68b4e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{7\\pi }{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121545/selection/28420441481517359a953269476eab72b5407e6c08575a9703d60f0a494468c5" :answer/id #uuid "f2ab487f-304a-5b85-8e84-4a65202a28aa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{6\\pi }{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121545/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "843d392a-3e80-5b0d-b9e3-6e9c678a8807" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-121545/selection/2bc5d83371a24844476947c013c304745bdc01e4bc7ab45335b74b409478e254" :answer-field/choices ["q-121545/selection/0f2229a8d284b0e3be30b8a234f6bf87fcbd918a8d02f5bb5f6312388d0ca00a" "q-121545/selection/8642f29c07ed588847b818ca52d7d9b13f60105c8ca35b3f5cb1a649a54ead1c" "q-121545/selection/2bc5d83371a24844476947c013c304745bdc01e4bc7ab45335b74b409478e254" "q-121545/selection/f877c20246cdffb02c0bf1049751cbded026a1167735517391df4b4eb845057e" "q-121545/selection/28420441481517359a953269476eab72b5407e6c08575a9703d60f0a494468c5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-121545" :question/id #uuid "57cf5fd6-82f4-5843-a107-b49508195a40" :question/math-academy-id "q-121545" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13952589/assets/0d956ac6b75c38bfbc5650966880a4eedaf69a0659407fb137d88d30fea08ab7.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the curve $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x$ and the line $y=-\\sqrt{3}.$ Find the $x$-coordinate of the point $A.$\n\n$$\n\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The $y$-values of both functions are the same at the intersection point. Equating the two equations gives: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=-\\sqrt{3}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-\\sqrt{3})=-\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis value lies inside $-\\frac{3\\pi }{2}<x<0.$ Hence, our first solution is ${x}_{1}=-\\frac{\\pi }{3}.$ This is the $x$ coordinate of $B.$\n\nTo get another solution, we add $-\\pi $ to the principal value. Thus,\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}=-\\pi +x=-\\pi -\\frac{\\pi }{3}=-\\frac{4\\pi }{3}.\n$$\n\nSo, the $x$-coordinate of $A$ is $-\\frac{4\\pi }{3}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-121545/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a71da663-e7a4-5781-973c-5dc7e4deb83f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-121545"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-322566/field-1/7b07fa4180fe9201f7944b6f4f5341acec086b4c50de2b4f4928478622402d76" :answer/id #uuid "82c42992-a302-59ce-8ec3-ea9527c718f7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{5\\pi}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-322566/field-1/438469ab2d71e1bb8b63f3164bacb1bbb54e29062b14dce6a666b63ac0081609" :answer/id #uuid "8514006d-99ea-5161-9f37-eb9f13dbd801" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-322566/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "355a0cc2-1961-59cb-a988-f660dbf176cc" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-322566/field-1/7b07fa4180fe9201f7944b6f4f5341acec086b4c50de2b4f4928478622402d76" :answer-field/choices ["q-322566/field-1/7b07fa4180fe9201f7944b6f4f5341acec086b4c50de2b4f4928478622402d76" "q-322566/field-1/438469ab2d71e1bb8b63f3164bacb1bbb54e29062b14dce6a666b63ac0081609"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-322566" :question/id #uuid "f3caba22-9915-504e-bd4c-02a454ebfe13" :question/math-academy-id "q-322566" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13952589/assets/024a7e545d37295878d7f32efd393310dcf1c2c9f88f124ffc5fe46b05155e2c.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the curve $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x$ and the line $y=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}.$\n\nThe **exact** value of the $x$-coordinate of the point $A$ is \n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The $y$-values of both functions are the same at the intersection point. Equating the two equations gives:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=arctan\\,(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3})=\\frac{\\pi }{6}\n$$\n\nThis value lies outside $-\\frac{3\\pi }{2}<x<-\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$ To get a value that's inside the required domain, we add $-\\pi $ to the principal value. Thus,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =x+(-\\pi ) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{6}-\\pi  \\\\  & =-\\frac{5\\pi }{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the $x$-coordinate of $A$ is $-\\frac{5\\pi }{6}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-322566/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a71da663-e7a4-5781-973c-5dc7e4deb83f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-322566"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-20482/selection/a3f72a33bd97dbcb26e67e320a072cf6fd98f5dc94f2de44db2fa04c176254bd" :answer/id #uuid "9caa6984-0aa0-5ce7-a4f5-c760d003359a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-20482/selection/03864569254141960db19b242c7f1e850d6147657a3c76f443bd0fefd8fede2f" :answer/id #uuid "1157eb80-1f9e-5b70-bdde-7143e7f7697a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5\\pi }{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-20482/selection/82f0679237d603c9b88d77fbc6f240065a24a3716631fab4d9f58426a7f011e5" :answer/id #uuid "c89c7f20-18a9-5905-8ec7-707cd71c6651" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-20482/selection/86ae4adf744f83815c6e176da09d1e1a7388c41a2337e3e7a6825862a8a438ec" :answer/id #uuid "5168d962-6b6d-597e-a9d7-70a2f777dfd4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4\\pi }{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-20482/selection/0f2229a8d284b0e3be30b8a234f6bf87fcbd918a8d02f5bb5f6312388d0ca00a" :answer/id #uuid "05a65956-3758-57b0-941c-0b7deac4b381" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{5\\pi }{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-20482/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "5366fc1f-4ae5-5a1a-bf03-f118b1c17f0b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-20482/selection/03864569254141960db19b242c7f1e850d6147657a3c76f443bd0fefd8fede2f" :answer-field/choices ["q-20482/selection/a3f72a33bd97dbcb26e67e320a072cf6fd98f5dc94f2de44db2fa04c176254bd" "q-20482/selection/03864569254141960db19b242c7f1e850d6147657a3c76f443bd0fefd8fede2f" "q-20482/selection/82f0679237d603c9b88d77fbc6f240065a24a3716631fab4d9f58426a7f011e5" "q-20482/selection/86ae4adf744f83815c6e176da09d1e1a7388c41a2337e3e7a6825862a8a438ec" "q-20482/selection/0f2229a8d284b0e3be30b8a234f6bf87fcbd918a8d02f5bb5f6312388d0ca00a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-20482" :question/id #uuid "7f77a0be-54c9-59a4-987f-02f55232c640" :question/math-academy-id "q-20482" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13952589/assets/95be2e7bf1dc425e0f0dd9ba818a6a06d0c9afc7874213194f68b1dd426cb110.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the curve $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x$ and the line $y=1.$ Find the $x$-coordinate of the point $B.$\n\n$$\n\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The $y$-values of both functions are the same at the intersection point. Equating the two equations gives: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=1\n$$\n\nNow, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(1)=\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis value lies inside $0\\le x\\le 2\\pi $ hence, our first solution is ${x}_{1}=\\frac{\\pi }{4}.$ This is the $x$ coordinate of $A.$\n\nTo get another solution, we add $\\pi $ to the principal value. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2}=\\pi +{x}_{1}=\\pi +\\frac{\\pi }{4}=\\frac{5\\pi }{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the $x$-coordinate of $B$ is $\\frac{5\\pi }{4}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-20482/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a71da663-e7a4-5781-973c-5